Page Structure for "Study in Canada"
✅ 1. Hero Section
Headline: "Study in Canada: Your Path to World-Class Education"
Brief Intro: A short paragraph about why Canada is a great study destination.
Call-to-Action (CTA) Button:
"Find Scholarships" → Links to available scholarships
"Apply Now" → Guide on application process
✅ 2. Why Study in Canada?
Key Benefits:

Affordable tuition & living costs compared to the US/UK
Post-graduation work permit (PGWP)
Safe, multicultural environment
High-ranking universities
Scholarship opportunities
Attractive icons for quick scanning.

✅ 3. Top Universities in Canada 🏫
A grid/list of top universities with links to their official pages.
Example:
🏅 University of Toronto
🏅 McGill University
🏅 University of British Columbia (UBC)
✅ 4. Admission Requirements & Process
Undergraduate & Postgraduate requirements
English/French Proficiency Exams (IELTS/TOEFL)
Application Deadlines
Step-by-step guide on how to apply
✅ 5. Scholarships & Funding 💰
List available scholarships for international students
Graduate Assistantships (GA, TA, RA)
Government-funded programs like Vanier Canada Graduate Scholarships
✅ 6. Student Visa Guide 🎫
Requirements to apply for a Canadian Study Permit
How to show proof of funds
Biometrics and medical exams
✅ 7. Cost of Living 💵
Breakdown of tuition fees, accommodation, food, and transportation
Tips on how students can save money
✅ 8. Work & Post-Graduation Opportunities 🏢
Can students work while studying? (Yes, up to 20 hours/week)
Post-Graduation Work Permit (PGWP): Stay & work after studies
✅ 9. Student Life in Canada 🇨🇦
Housing options (on-campus vs off-campus)
Best cities for students (Toronto, Vancouver, Montreal)
Student support groups & communities
✅ 10. How to Apply (Step-by-Step) 📝
Interactive checklist or step-by-step guide to make it actionable
✅ 11. Aarticles about Canada 📝
✅ 12. Hidden gem schools - affordable schools in canada📝
🔗 Additional UX Features
FAQs Section – Common student questions answered.
Live Chat / Contact Support – To guide students who need help.
Success Stories – Testimonials from African students in Canada.
Resources Section – Downloadable guides, application templates, etc.


Final Database Schema Recommendation
Main Tables
study_destinations

id (PK)
country (e.g., "Canada")
flag_code (e.g., "CA")
image_url
href (e.g., "/study/canada")
universities

id (PK)
name (e.g., "University of Toronto")
website
study_destination_id (FK → study_destinations)
admission_requirements

id (PK)
requirement (Text)
program_id (FK → programs)
university_id (M2M → universities)
programs (for undergrad, master's, PhD)

id (PK)
level (e.g., "Undergraduate", "Master's", "PhD")
cost_of_living

id (PK)
study_destination_id (FK → study_destinations)
average_rent
food_expenses
transportation_costs
tuition_fees
work_opportunities

id (PK)
study_destination_id (FK → study_destinations)
can_work_while_studying (Boolean)
max_hours_per_week
post_graduation_work_permit (Text)
student_life

id (PK)
study_destination_id (FK → study_destinations)
best_cities_for_students (Text)
housing_options (Text)
student_support_groups (Text)